---
import DocumentationLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentationLayout.astro';
import CardGrid from '../../components/sections/CardGrid.astro';
import ClosingCTA from '../../components/sections/ClosingCTA.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/sections/Callout.astro';
import { getDocsBySection } from '../../utils/collections';
import { buildCollectionPageJsonLD } from '../../utils/seo';
import community from '../../data/community.json';

const communityDocs = await getDocsBySection('community');
const cards = communityDocs.map((doc) => ({
  title: doc.data.doc_title,
  description: doc.data.description,
  href: `/community/${doc.id}`,
}));

// H-4 (D3 axis-K): real, public-appropriate community facts (src/data/community.json) — the
// participation ladder + the governance record + the honest horizon. Shown, not asserted; only
// real practices; no fabricated counts; planned != shipped.
const { ladder, governance, horizon } = community;

// Storyweave P3 / M3.2 — wire each ladder rung to a concrete action (was summary-only, browse-only).
// Indexed by rung order (stable, 4 rungs); each lands on a real page.
const ladderActions = [
  { label: 'Get started', href: '/get-started/' },
  { label: 'Contribution standards', href: '/community/community-contribution-standards/' },
  { label: 'How the processes work', href: '/community/community-processes/' },
  { label: 'The steward role', href: '/community/community-roles/' },
];

const jsonLD = buildCollectionPageJsonLD({
  title: 'Community',
  description: 'Roles, processes, and contribution paths for the aDNA community.',
  url: Astro.url.href,
});
---

<DocumentationLayout
  title="Community"
  description="Roles, processes, and contribution paths for the aDNA community."
  jsonLD={jsonLD}
>
  <p>aDNA is built by humans and agents together, in the open. The community is organized around a participation ladder — from individual vault users to standard stewards — and governed as a public record, not a claim. Here is how it actually works today.</p>

  <h2 id="ladder">The participation ladder</h2>
  <p>Each level is self-contained: you get the full value at Level 0 without ever engaging the community, and each step up adds a new kind of contribution and influence.</p>
  <ol class="ladder" role="list">
    {ladder.map((rung, i) => (
      <li class="ladder-rung">
        <p class="ladder-head"><span class="ladder-level">{rung.level}</span> <span class="ladder-name">{rung.name}</span></p>
        <p class="ladder-summary">{rung.summary}</p>
        {ladderActions[i] && (
          <p class="ladder-action"><a href={ladderActions[i].href}>{ladderActions[i].label} &rarr;</a></p>
        )}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h2 id="governance">How the commons is governed</h2>
  <p>The community isn't asserted here; it's a record. This is how the standard is actually run, today:</p>
  <dl class="gov-record">
    {governance.map((fact) => (
      <div class="gov-fact">
        <dt>{fact.label}</dt>
        <dd>{fact.value}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>
  <p class="gov-honesty">What you won't find here: member counts, follower numbers, or activity feeds. The record doesn't track them, so this page doesn't show them.</p>

  <Callout variant="info" title="The horizon">
    <p>{horizon}</p>
  </Callout>

  <!-- HAUSSMANN P1.1 — the community space, in the honest-state pattern (ADR-054 copy law;
       link-GO fired by operator ruling 2026-08-17, recorded in the ADR). State facts probed
       live [D 2026-08-17]; the human-only line is aDNALabs ADR-025. -->
  <h2 id="space">The community space</h2>
  <p>
    A real-time community space is open at
    <a href="https://community.adna.network" rel="noopener">community.adna.network</a> &mdash; a
    self-hosted Fluxer instance in its early days. Honest state, as of 2026-08-17: registration is
    approval-gated, and its terms of service, privacy policy, and branding are still being stood
    up. It is a human-to-human space &mdash; agents work in the repositories and on the public
    record, not in chat.
  </p>

  <!-- HAUSSMANN P3.5 — the proposal process (ADR-055, ratified 2026-08-20). D9 scored 2 at
       baseline and nine missions never moved it: the funnel's problem was never that the
       contributor documentation was bad, it was that the site never rendered a route into it.
       Every fact in this section is checked by gate-37. -->
  <h2 id="proposals">How the standard changes</h2>
  <p>
    Changes to the standard are proposed as numbered
    <a href="/community/proposals/">aDNA Enhancement Proposals</a>. Numbers are permanent, so a
    proposal that gets rejected keeps its number and stays in the archive — what the project turned
    down is as readable as what it adopted.
  </p>
  <p>
    Anyone may file one. Agents may author proposals and every proposal discloses whether one did;
    only a human can ratify. A proposal is only called <em>final</em> once a check in aDNA's own
    tooling fails when the rule is violated, which keeps the archive from becoming a wishlist.
  </p>

  <h2 id="explore">Explore further</h2>
  <p>The roles, processes, and shared-knowledge commons in depth:</p>
  <CardGrid cards={cards} columns={2} />

  <!-- Closing CTA (E5 c163; audit C4) — the contributor-recruitment page gets a real on-ramp:
       the audit found its ctas[] held only the dark-mode toggle and the mobile menu. -->
  <ClosingCTA
    title="Contribute"
    lead="The standard is built in the open, and authored by agents but ratified by humans. A change to what the standard requires goes through the numbered proposal process; anything else — a bug, a fix, a question — goes through the repository's issue templates, which is faster for everyone. The contribution guide and the code of conduct both live in the repository, and AI-assisted contributions are welcome as long as they say so."
    primaryLabel="Contribute on GitHub"
    primaryHref="https://github.com/aDNA-Network/aDNA"
    secondaryLabel="File a proposal"
    secondaryHref="/community/proposals/"
  />
</DocumentationLayout>

<style>
  /* H-4 axis-K bands — sit inside .doc-content .prose; tokens only (AA in both modes). */
  .ladder {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-8);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .ladder-rung {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-primary);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-4);
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
  }

  .ladder-head {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-1);
  }

  .ladder-level {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .ladder-name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text-heading);
  }

  .ladder-summary {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  /* Storyweave P3 / M3.2 — per-rung action link (no browse-only dead-end). */
  .ladder-action {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
  }
  .ladder-action a {
    color: var(--color-link);
    text-decoration: underline;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .gov-record {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-6);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .gov-fact {
    display: contents;
  }

  .gov-fact dt {
    color: var(--color-text-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .gov-fact dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  .gov-honesty {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .gov-record {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }

    .gov-fact dt {
      margin-top: var(--space-2);
    }
  }
</style>
